WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
In a Vatican museum stands a stone coffin,

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.450
carved in Rome around the year 350.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.230
It shows Jesus' last hours.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.850
Yet there is no crucified body.

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.930
In some churches in Lent, a huge
painted cloth hangs before the altar.

6
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.100
At Easter, a tall candle
is marked with a cross,

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.070
two Greek letters and this year.

8
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.380
So how can a candle, a stone coffin or a
cloth tell people what Catholics believe

9
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.830
about death?

10
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.720
In this mission, you'll
decode objects like these,

11
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.530
one symbol at a time.

12
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.930
Then you'll weigh up a claim: that
objects and images teach faith better than

13
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.030
words.

14
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: find out how these objects
show what Catholics believe about death.
